  "prefLabel": "He-C 5010.01 Purpose",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-C 5010.01 Purpose. The purpose of these rules is to describe the establishment and operation of the New Hampshire drug use review board (DUR board), created to comply with federal requirements of Section 4401 of the Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1990 relative to pharmaceutical services furnished under the medicaid fee for service (FFS) program and to comply with Chapter 19 Laws of New Hampshire (2009).\n\nSource. #5529, eff 12-16-92; ss by #6907, eff 12-9-98; ss by #8743, eff 10-24-06; ss by #9587, eff 11-4-09; ss by #12460, eff 1-13-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-c5000.html"
